// `emit_rep.vl` — `repOf`: the unified wasm-rep descriptor, derived structurally from
// the checker's `Ty` arena (ROADMAP "repOf unification"), replacing five parallel
// schemes that must otherwise agree by convention (`VKind`, raw field codes,
// `$fnsig` tokens, `fRetKind`, the side enums) — each a place a rep bug can drift
// from its twins. Consumers migrate site by site under the fixpoint, corpus and
// rep-fuzzer gates.
//
// Coverage is deliberately partial (`rdCovered`): an arm is marked covered only
// where the arena decides the rep exactly as the emitter's legacy classifier does;
// everything else returns `rdCovered == 0` and the consumer keeps its name-based
// path, widening arm by arm. Recursive types are real arena cycles: the canonical
// structural key (`repCanonKey`) terminates them with a de-Bruijn back-edge.

